 ## Background
-Mie theory describes the scattering of electromagnetic radiation by spherical particles [S1]. The implementation used in this context is based on Bohren and Huffman's [BH83] code, widely regarded as the standard reference for Mie scattering calculations. Philip Laven’s MiePlot [Lav] provides a practical implementation of this theory for atmospheric phenomena. The specific application to cloud and rain particles uses lognormal size distributions described by Pruppacher and Klett [PK00].
